# Python virtualenvs. A venv is tens of thousands of library files and is
# rebuilt from requirements, never committed - the node_modules of Python.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Runtime logs. Langflow rewrites 09_LangFlow/langflow.log on every run and it
# reached 13 MB in two days, which is noise in a diff and nothing a reader needs
# a year from now. The workflow and flow exports are the artefacts worth keeping.
*.log

